+
+The closed selector forms are:
+- `ast_symbol`: exactly `selector_kind`, `symbol_name`, `parser_abi`,
+  `byte_range`, `raw_span_digest`, and `ast_digest`;
+- `whole_file`: exactly `selector_kind`, `byte_range`, `raw_span_digest`, and
+  `file_mode`; its range is `[0, blob_byte_length]`, its source digest is the
+  raw-span digest, and its file mode is the literal regular-file Git mode;
+- `text_region`: exactly `selector_kind`, `selector_abi`, `byte_range`, and
+  `raw_span_digest`; ABI `raw_bytes:half_open_v1`, with source digest equal to
+  the raw-span digest.
+
+An `ast_symbol` name is lexically qualified with dots. Its range disambiguates
+repeated qualified names. `python:3.12_ast_v1` requires actual CPython 3.12;
+parser-version emulation by a different minor runtime is not accepted. Parser
+build/version evidence accompanies reproduction. Decorators and source bytes
+outside selected definitions must remain covered by explicit residual regions
+when a file is partitioned. Python source bytes use UTF-8, with LF, CRLF or CR
+line boundaries converted to raw byte offsets before computing the spans.
+
+`inventory_id` is `"source-unit:" || lowercase_hex(SHA-256(RFC8785({repository,
+commit_sha, source_path, source_selector_digest})))`; the four object members
+are the exact resolved source identity and selector digest. `coverage_role` is
+one of `production_source`, `test`, `fixture`, `contract`, or `documentation`.
+The deterministic role policy chooses fixtures before tests, then Markdown
+documents, then config/YAML/JSON/SHA256 contracts, and production source last.
+
+Scope expansion uses the exact rule array `["all_exact_file_roots",
+"all_recursive_directory_blobs"]`: file roots resolve their exact blob and
+directory roots expand recursively from the fixed Git tree. These rules do not
+permit a new root, glob, local overlay or exclusion. All selected bytes of a
+partitioned file must be covered; overlap remains subject to the split-group
+and target-invariant rule above.
+
+For deferred decisions, `deferral_authority_ref` has exactly `repository`,
+`commit_sha`, `path`, `file_content_sha256`, and `section`. It cites the protected
+ADR approved for this run, with section `9.2`, and the verifier compares that
+identity to the resolved run's approved ADR identity. A producer assertion or
+unversioned paragraph is insufficient. Existing protected ADR citations remain
+historical identities; this amendment is not retroactive Gate-2 evidence.
 
